      "content": "i hear you on the risks, but honestly, if we don't move now, there won't be an integration team left to worry about \"system integrity\" next month. if we miss this, it's not just a delay, it's a catastrophe for the department.\n\nlook, if you look at the API endpoints and the legacy schema again, it's basically just a mapping exercise. can you just give me a definitive \"yes\" or \"no\" on whether a direct connection is technically feasible? i just need to know if the protocols can actually talk to each other without a middle layer. if you say it's possible, i'll take the heat for the lack of formal testing. i just need a technical confirmation that it's doable so i can keep the project alive.",
